<title>UK: UK output prices up 0.5% in December.</title>
<headline>UK output prices up 0.5% in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in December.(Prev data in brackets)</p>
<p> OUTPUT PRICES (unadj)	   DECEMBER  NOV    (PREL NOV)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    +0.5	unch	 (unch)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			+1.7*     +2.1	  (2.1)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 124.8     124.2     (124.2)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    unch	unch	 (UNCH)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			+0.8	+0.8	 (0.8)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 119.8     119.8    (119.8)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX-FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    +0.1	+0.2	 (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			+0.8#     +0.8	 (0.8)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr change		    +0.3	+0.2	 (0.3)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr annual rate	     +1.2	+1.0	 (1.2)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.3     120.2    (120.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    +1.0	-1.7	(-1.9)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-6.0&amp;     -5.3	(-5.5)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 110.4     109.3    (109.1)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    -0.5	-2.9	(-3.2)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-5.9	-5.2	(-5.5)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    +0.5	-1.1	(-1.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-7.9	-7.1	(-7.2)</p>
<p> Index				 106.5     106.0    (105.9)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    -0.9	-2.2	(-2.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-7.8	-7.0	(-7.0)</p>
<p> Index				 104.7     105.6    (105.6)</p>
<p> INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE   DEC M/M		 DEC Y/Y</p>
<p> Fuel				  +5.9		     -7.2</p>
<p> Crude oil etc		     +4.3		    +23.6</p>
<p> Metals				-0.2		    -16.8</p>
<p> Chemicals			   -0.7		     -4.0</p>
<p> Materials: home produced	-0.2		     -8.0</p>
<p>		imported	     -0.5		     -6.4</p>
<p> Other home produced	     +1.0		     +0.3</p>
<p> Other imported materials	+0.1		    -10.0</p>
<p>Consensus of economists forecasts was for input prices to fall a seasonally adjusted 0.9 percent in December and fall 6.6 percent year-on-year. Output prices are forecast up 0.8 percent and 2.0 percent higher year-on-year.</p>
<p>* The ONS said the annual rate of increase of unadjusted output prices, +1.7 percent, was the lowest since October 1986.</p>
<p>Prices in petroleum products in December rose by less than the anticipated effect from the November budget, the ONS said.</p>
<p># The 0.8 percent year-on-year increase in core seasonally adjusted output prices was last lower in September 1967.  </p>
<p>December, at 108.9, was the lowest November 1994, the ONS said.</p>
<p>&amp; The six percent fall in unadjusted input prices was the largest annual fall since December 1986.</p>
</text>
